( chess pieces: constants and the sheet lookup. The art itself is
  studio data — sprites `pieces` (4x3 sheet, one 8x8 cell per piece:
  white P N B R Q K, then black), `squares`, `dot` and `cursor`, and
  the scenes `board` / `setup` — exported to assets.ux, which main.ux
  imports first. Edit them in uxn-forge's Chess example (Sprites and
  Scene views) and re-export; this file never holds pixels. )

PT_PAWN :: 0;
PT_KNIGHT :: 1;
PT_BISHOP :: 2;
PT_ROOK :: 3;
PT_QUEEN :: 4;
PT_KING :: 5;

( Piece codes on the board: 0 empty, 1-6 white P N B R Q K,
  7-12 black. A piece's sheet cell is code - 1. )
PC_EMPTY :: 0;

( Varvara blends per side, same as the setup scene's nodes. White
  0: 1 -> orange fill, 2 -> black rim, 0 clear. Black 5: identity,
  1 -> black fill, 3 -> dark-blue rim, 0 clear. )
PIECE_BLEND_W :: 0;
PIECE_BLEND_B :: 5;

( ROM address of a side/kind tile (kind 0-5, side 0 white): sheet
  cells are 16 bytes each, row-major. )
tile_addr :: fn(kind: u8, side: u8) -> u16 {
    return &spr_pieces + (side * 6 + kind) * 16;
}

( Screen.sprite byte for a piece: 2bpp + the side's blend, plus both
  flips (rotated 180) when it belongs to the far side. Arithmetic,
  no locals: zero-page is the scarce resource here. )
piece_mode :: fn(side: u8, far: u8) -> u8 {
    return 128 + PIECE_BLEND_W + side * (PIECE_BLEND_B - PIECE_BLEND_W) + far * 48;
}
